  "config.page.confront": "Confrontations (saturation)",
  "config.page.confront.tip": "NPCs walk up to you when what they saw piles up.",
  "config.confront.intro": "Every memory an NPC witnesses feeds one or more feelings, each with its own score. The same round of drinks can amuse one neighbour, please another and worry a third. Each feeling drains on its own clock and, once it passes a level, makes that NPC want a word: they show their bubble and open a normal AliveNpcs conversation already knowing why. When several are ready at once, the turn goes to whoever is closest, feels it most strongly, and holds the weightier feeling; the rest keep it for the next time you talk to them. Friendship is never touched by AliveSensor.",
  "config.confront.enabled.name": "NPCs confront the farmer",
  "config.confront.maxReactions.name": "NPCs who can react to one event",
  "config.confront.maxReactions.tip": "Each reaction is an AI call. Beyond this many, the others don't come over; they bring it up the next time you talk to them, which costs nothing.",
  "config.confront.section.meters": "Feelings (edit assets/meters.json)",
  "config.confront.meters.intro": "How much each event feeds each feeling lives in assets/event-types.json, and the feelings themselves — levels, how fast they fade, which bubble they show — in assets/meters.json. Both are plain JSON you can edit or add to without touching the mod.",
